  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "SNMP: Fix checking of SNMP v3 auth if MD5 method is used",
  "description": "When the user enters row to SNMP Users table in wireshark and Authentication model is set to MD5, row is ignored in processing. The reason is that constant for MD5 is 0, but the code checks if the value is defined by simple 'usm_p.user_assoc' condition. Therefore 0 never succeeds.\nAs item can have only listed values, I think the check can be removed.\nFunction verified on sample.\n\nI propose to cherry pick the change to all stable branches.\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit 7f376c7ced445c6373098b8f7f8790a78822fe0a)",
